			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for native dialog interactivity\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from 70e79155 to 6e6a6c5 to synchronize the latest revisions for Cocoon and Mountain on the Current branch.\n\n**Cocoon:** Consolidate fragmented window message handling into a single `Window.ShowMessage` gRPC method, delegating action button rendering to Mountain. Enhance URI resolution to explicitly validate `scheme`, `authority`, and `path` properties to prevent broken icon paths.\n\n**Mountain:** Standardize Tauri event naming to PascalCase (e.g., `postMessage`) and refactor `Window.ShowMessage` to use atomic sequence counters. This enables blocking behavior that renders action buttons in the native UI and awaits user selection.\n\nThese changes ensure consistent event naming, prevent illegal event crashes, and restore full interactivity for notification actions across the extension host IPC layer.",
			"SHA": "059ed59eab25c6f01cef5659514630c910180c20"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:40:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for URI lifecycle and browser view preparation\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from 4b0d889a to 70e79155 to synchronize the latest revisions for Mountain and Wind on the Current branch.\n\n**Mountain:** Implement gRPC notification handlers for `UnregisterExternalUriOpener` and `UnregisterRemoteAuthorityResolver` within the Vine protocol. These handlers leverage existing `UnregisterByHandle` utilities to ensure consistent lifecycle management for remote authority and URI opener extensions.\n\n**Wind:** Expand the `StubChannels` registry in `TauriMainProcessService` to include definitions for the `browserViewGroup` service. Add stubs for `updateKeybindings`, `updateTheme`, `updateConfiguration`, `getBrowserViews`, and dev tools commands to establish the contract for upcoming native browser view operations.\n\nThese changes ensure full lifecycle support for extension URI handlers and lay the groundwork for advanced view management in the Workbench service layer.",
			"SHA": "c4db0cd318e34bd96e288b5ebc3e0322026b03e7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:36:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for URI robustness in Cocoon and Sky\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule to commit 4b0d889a, addressing URI reconstruction issues across the gRPC bridge and Source Control Manager layers.\n\n**Cocoon:** Replace reliance on default `.toString()` and `.external` properties with explicit structural checks for `scheme`, `authority`, and `path`. This ensures valid URI strings are constructed and transmitted to Mountain, preventing malformed requests in document and notification flows.\n\n**Sky:** Refine URI parsing in `InstallScm.ts` to distinguish custom URI stringification from default `Object.prototype` methods. This prevents generic objects from triggering false positives during immediate service execution, aligning with the simplified bridge logic.\n\nThese changes restore stability in file access, language provider invocations, and source control operations by guaranteeing accurate type handling and robust request routing.",
			"SHA": "09652f8f2c47a788f358a6e272d24e5c27e5d006"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:26:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for URI robustness in Cocoon and Sky\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from 1b955092 to 0e9defee to address URI reconstruction issues across the gRPC bridge and Source Control Manager layers.\n\n**Cocoon:** Replace reliance on default `.toString()` and `.external` properties with explicit structural checks for `scheme`, `authority`, and `path`. This ensures valid URI strings are constructed and transmitted to Mountain, preventing malformed requests in document and notification flows.\n\n**Sky:** Refine URI parsing in `InstallScm.ts` to distinguish custom URI stringification from default `Object.prototype` methods. This prevents generic objects from triggering false positives during immediate service execution, aligning with the simplified bridge logic.\n\nThese changes restore stability in file access, language provider invocations, and source control operations by guaranteeing accurate type handling and robust request routing.",
			"SHA": "acfbccb9ed93dab7082fe980ac9acff450c35b9a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:20:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for storage expansion and dialog fixes\n\nUpdate the `Element` git submodule from `feccffc3` to `1b955092` to synchronize the latest revisions for `Cocoon`, `Mountain`, and `Sky` on the Current branch.\n\n**Cocoon:** Introduce the `Storage.GetItems` RPC method to support bulk retrieval and refactor URI resolution logic to explicitly validate `scheme`, `authority`, and `path` properties, preventing malformed URIs during request routing.\n\n**Mountain:** Fix `ShowMessageBox` to correctly concatenate title and detail text for native dialog usability and correct `QuickInputShowQuickPick` to preserve multi-select return arrays. Remove the obsolete `showTextDocument` handler from IPC routing now that Sky handles this natively.\n\n**Sky:** Modify `BakeExtensionManifest` to detect and invalidate cache stubs with zero extension counts, preventing build hangs caused by stale empty records.\n\nThese changes ensure robust storage handling, accurate user dialog behavior, and reliable extension metadata generation during the bootstrap sequence.",
			"SHA": "0a4bde413b3dfbfe6ee987002d20304c6618f4a4"
		}
	],
